WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.030 --> 00:00:01.430
- It can't be that hard, right?

00:00:01.430 --> 00:00:02.950
It's just a little bit of hair.

00:00:02.950 --> 00:00:04.011
- Ouch!

00:00:04.011 --> 00:00:05.450
- Oh no, oh no!

00:00:10.260 --> 00:00:13.650
- A lot of my coworkers
have been pressuring me

00:00:13.650 --> 00:00:15.530
into doing stuff with my eyebrows.

00:00:15.530 --> 00:00:17.850
- I've gotten them waxed like once,

00:00:17.850 --> 00:00:19.891
probably when I was like 13.

00:00:19.891 --> 00:00:23.710
- I get, from my Hispanic
heritage, the uni-brow.

00:00:23.710 --> 00:00:25.950
- This is like the cumulation of like

00:00:25.950 --> 00:00:29.430
me going into surgery
and not being a doctor

00:00:29.430 --> 00:00:32.040
and having to, you know,
take out someone's heart.

00:00:32.040 --> 00:00:33.870
- I have no idea what I'm doing.

00:00:33.870 --> 00:00:36.120
- These hairs on the edge,
they start to get very faint,

00:00:36.120 --> 00:00:37.220
but they keep going.

00:00:37.220 --> 00:00:38.330
If there's an especially dark one,

00:00:38.330 --> 00:00:39.680
like that one right there, boom!

00:00:39.680 --> 00:00:40.561
What the heck?

00:00:40.561 --> 00:00:42.230
- Is my skin supposed to stretch this far?

00:00:42.230 --> 00:00:43.311
I literally am like...

00:00:44.781 --> 00:00:45.435
(light ding)

00:00:45.435 --> 00:00:46.545
- Oh my goodness.

00:00:46.545 --> 00:00:48.185
- Ow, ow, ow!

00:00:48.185 --> 00:00:49.685
Where should I put the hair?

00:00:49.685 --> 00:00:51.495
- There's like meat on
the end of the hair.

00:00:51.495 --> 00:00:53.565
- Boom, look at that.

00:00:53.565 --> 00:00:55.765
That's a hair, like on top of a head.

00:00:56.905 --> 00:00:58.495
- So do I keep it here and then cut it,

00:00:58.495 --> 00:00:59.545
or do I--
- [Man] Yeah.

00:00:59.545 --> 00:01:01.655
- Okay guys.

00:01:03.135 --> 00:01:05.265
How is it? Yeah?

00:01:05.265 --> 00:01:07.805
These really tiny tools,
I feel like small children

00:01:07.805 --> 00:01:09.474
are supposed to like operate these.

00:01:09.474 --> 00:01:11.445
- Try not to stab myself.

00:01:11.445 --> 00:01:13.095
- This is literally like defusing a bomb.

00:01:13.095 --> 00:01:15.525
Like if you go too far,
you know, you're dead.

00:01:15.525 --> 00:01:16.745
- It's like an afro pick.

00:01:16.745 --> 00:01:19.325
I don't know how I decide
how much to cut with this.

00:01:20.905 --> 00:01:24.218
- It looks like a Crayola
crayon, but it's for your face.

00:01:24.218 --> 00:01:27.117
- I fear I might have
chosen the wrong color,

00:01:27.117 --> 00:01:29.117
because it's really
showing up a lot lighter.

00:01:29.117 --> 00:01:30.858
- Is it like skin tone or hair color

00:01:30.858 --> 00:01:32.007
that I'm trying to match here?

00:01:32.978 --> 00:01:34.107
- Oh that's a lot.

00:01:35.137 --> 00:01:35.967
- (laughs)

00:01:36.177 --> 00:01:37.417
- I don't think it's doing anything.

00:01:37.417 --> 00:01:39.817
- Oh shit, that's hilarious.

00:01:39.817 --> 00:01:41.897
- That is a glistening looking eyebrow.

00:01:41.897 --> 00:01:44.568
- That is intense.

00:01:44.568 --> 00:01:47.158
Black was not the way to go.

00:01:48.568 --> 00:01:50.939
- I feel like I took
Ron Swanson's mustache

00:01:50.939 --> 00:01:53.788
and stuck them like above my eyeballs.

00:01:55.378 --> 00:01:57.388
- I think they look good.

00:01:59.818 --> 00:02:02.499
- I will probably not
groom my eyebrows again,

00:02:02.499 --> 00:02:06.319
unless I get, you know, more
torture from my coworkers.

00:02:06.319 --> 00:02:07.718
- I will never do this again.

00:02:07.718 --> 00:02:10.178
- You can (bleep) with trimming
it out, grooming it down,

00:02:10.178 --> 00:02:11.538
you know, thinning it out, or you can just

00:02:11.538 --> 00:02:13.458
color in all the bad parts with a pencil.

00:02:13.458 --> 00:02:15.068
- That whole like, (hums).

00:02:15.068 --> 00:02:16.718
Is that an official,
like, way to make your

00:02:16.718 --> 00:02:18.448
eyebrows look prettier? This thing?

